{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784647569,"nonce":"lfcoDCkcqxeItmh2/nUfndVlouY=","message":"## Root-cause analysis\n\nThe base commit shown before applying is produced by two disjoint branches\nof the checkout flow (`src/b4/review_tui/_tracking_app.py` ~1613-1655), and\nthey render the base in two different formats — neither of which includes\nthe commit subject. The \"randomness\" Mark observed is fully determined by\nwhether the series declares its own base.\n\n**1. Series-specified base.** If the series carries a `base-commit:`\ntrailer (`lser.base_commit`), the hint is built as\n`Series base: {bc[:12]}` (`_tracking_app.py:1616-1618`) — a bare truncated\nSHA. This is the \"just the commit hash\" case (the tegra_warn series pins a\n-next base).\n\n**2. Guessed base.** With no base-commit trailer, `lser.find_base()`\n(`_tracking_app.py:1634`) is consulted; it returns a git *describe* name\n(e.g. `heads/foo`, `v6.15-rc4-123-g…`), rendered as\n`Guessed base: {guessed} (exact match | N/M blobs)`. This is the\n\"git describe\" case.\n\nSo the format isn't random — it's a clean bifurcation on presence of the\nbase-commit trailer. Critically, **neither branch ever resolves the base to\nits commit subject** (no `git show -s --format=%s` / `log --oneline`), so\nthe reviewer can't judge whether the base is an appropriate merge point —\nwhich is precisely the check Mark wants for series that may get merged.\n\nSeparately, the persistent detail panel (`_show_details`,\n`_tracking_app.py:1962-2092`) has **no base row at all** — the base is only\never surfaced transiently, inside the checkout confirmation hint.\n\n## Related bugs\n\nOverlaps `bd95e9f`: the base is not shown in the standing UI, and when a\nseries specifies no base it is resolved lazily to the *moving* target-branch\nHEAD at apply time (`_tracking_app.py:2765-2773`). Together they cover the\n\"what base, and is it the right one?\" gap — this bug is the display-format\nhalf, `bd95e9f` the resolution/visibility half.","files":null}]}